<h2>Part 9. Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Not counting bags.</strong> Count bags, not just people.</li>
<li><strong>Overfilling the vehicle.</strong> Seventeen is the limit.</li>
<li><strong>Comparing only the per-km rate.</strong> Compare the daily minimum, Bata and extras.</li>
<li><strong>Underestimating stop time.</strong> Add an hour for a group of 17.</li>
<li><strong>A late return.</strong> Extra Bata applies after 10:00 PM, and tired drivers are a risk.</li>
<li><strong>Skipping the written quotation.</strong> A phone price is not a contract.</li>
<li><strong>No coordinator.</strong> One organised person prevents most arguments.</li>
<li><strong>Forgetting interstate permits.</strong> Tell us your whole route.</li>
<li><strong>Ignoring AC for long summer trips.</strong> The small saving is rarely worth the discomfort.</li>
<li><strong>Booking late for peak dates.</strong> The fleet fills up.</li>
</ol>

